<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH JULY REAL FARM REVENUE FALLS 18.5PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>CZECH JULY REAL FARM REVENUE FALLS 18.5PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total revenues, in inflation adjusted terms, from Czech farming enterprises fell 18.5 percent year-on-year in July, putting revenues for January-July down 2.5 percent, the Czech Statistical Office said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The statistical office added that the number of workers employed in the agricultural sector rose in absolute terms to 146,976 from 144,575 in the previous month but was some 5.9 percent lower than in July 1995. The average monthly farm wage was 8,231 crowns, up from 7,690 in June the office added.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
